ndergraduate\nGraduate\nResources\nLinks\nHome\nGraduate\nApplication Procedure\nAAA\nGraduate Mathematics Application Procedure\nProgram Requirements\nPh.D. Program Timeline\nApplication Procedure\nFunding\nApplied Mathematics\nMaster of Science in Mathematical Finance\nCourse Descriptions and Current Offerings\nGraduate Placement\nGraduate Student Seminars\nList of Application Materials\nApplication for admission: apply online (The application fee is $85.00.)\nApplication for teaching assistantship and fellowship: download form\n3 letters of recommendation: download form\nOfficial transcripts from all undergraduate institutions attended (including exchange student study).\nTOEFL (Test of English as a Foreign Language) for students whose native language is not English, including those applying for transfer from U.S. institutions\nApplicants who submit a TOEFL score of at least 550 on the paper-based test, or 213 on the computer-based test, will not be required to take any courses in English as a second language.\nFor full consideration for a teaching assistantship we encourage applicants to have all application materials submitted by January 15 (if from the US) and February 15 (if from outside of the US).\nTo be considered for a University Fellowship all application materials must be submitted by January 1.\nApplication materials should be sent to:\nGraduate Admissions\nDepartment of Mathematics\nUniversity of Miami\nP.O. Box 249085\nCoral Gables, Florida 33124-4250\nNote that the GRE test is accepted but not required. Your GRE scores can be at most 5 years old. Please plan your GRE test dates so that the scores will be reported in time for the January deadline!\nPlease contact math@math.miami.edu with any questions about this procedure.\nTop\nUniversity of Miami\nCoral Gables, FL 33124\n305-284-2211\nDepartment of Mathematics\n1365 Memorial Drive\nUngar 515\nCoral Gables,\nFL\n33146\nPhone:\n305.284.2575\nPhone:\n305.284.2575\nFax::\n305.284.2848\nEmail:\nmath@mat